      "text": "Mutant knots and intersection graphs — We prove that if a ﬁnite order knot invariant does not disting uish mutant knots, then the corresponding weight system depends on the interse ction graph of a\n\n**Mutant knots and intersection graphs**\n\n*S. V. Chmutov ∗, S. K. Lando †*\n\n13 pp, 10 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We prove that if a ﬁnite order knot invariant does not disting uish mutant knots, then the corresponding weight system depends on the interse ction graph of a chord diagram rather than on the diagram itself. The convers e statement is easy and well known. We discuss relationship between our res ults and certain Lie algebra weight systems.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Introduction; Proof; Representability of graphs as the intersection; Proof of Theorem ??; Lie algebra weight systems and intersection gr; Weight systems via Lie algebras; The 4-bialgebra of graphs; The sl(2) weight system; The gl(1|1) weight system\n\n**Extracted claims (proposals, not verified).**\n- Theorem 1: If a ﬁnite order knot invariant does not distinguish mutants , then the\n- Theorem 2: Two chord diagrams have the same intersection graph if and on ly if they\n- Theorem 3: The universal weight systems associated to the Lie algebra sl(2) and\n- Theorem 4: The universal weight system associated to the Lie algebra sl(2) depends\n- Theorem 5: The universal weight systems associated to the Lie superalg ebra gl(1|1)\n- Theorem 3: Consider the part C2 participating in the Whitney twist and apply to",
